{
 "subs": [
  {
   "text": "At 3:14 and 7 seconds, every clock on Earth",
   "t0": 2,
   "t1": 5.152,
   "end": 5.402,
   "n": 35
  },
  {
   "text": "skipped the same second.",
   "t0": 5.402,
   "t1": 7.346,
   "end": 9.796,
   "n": 21
  },
  {
   "text": "Phones.",
   "t0": 10.296,
   "t1": 10.667,
   "end": 10.917,
   "n": 7
  },
  {
   "text": "Train stations.",
   "t0": 10.917,
   "t1": 11.878,
   "end": 12.128,
   "n": 14
  },
  {
   "text": "Wristwatches.",
   "t0": 12.248,
   "t1": 13.152,
   "end": 13.402,
   "n": 13
  },
  {
   "text": "All of them.",
   "t0": 13.402,
   "t1": 14.467,
   "end": 16.167,
   "n": 10
  },
  {
   "text": "The atomic clocks in Colorado, Paris and Tokyo confirmed it.",
   "t0": 16.667,
   "t1": 20.717,
   "end": 22.417,
   "n": 51
  },
  {
   "text": "Exactly one second was gone.",
   "t0": 22.917,
   "t1": 24.789,
   "end": 25.039,
   "n": 24
  },
  {
   "text": "Not lost, removed.",
   "t0": 25.039,
   "t1": 26.328,
   "end": 28.578,
   "n": 16
  },
  {
   "text": "Every government asked the same question.",
   "t0": 29.078,
   "t1": 31.438,
   "end": 31.688,
   "n": 36
  },
  {
   "text": "Where did it go?",
   "t0": 31.688,
   "t1": 32.707,
   "end": 35.157,
   "n": 13
  },
  {
   "text": "But the strangest part wasn't the missing second.",
   "t0": 35.657,
   "t1": 38.702,
   "end": 40.402,
   "n": 42
  },
  {
   "text": "It was that the cameras kept recording through it.",
   "t0": 40.902,
   "t1": 43.575,
   "end": 45.425,
   "n": 42
  },
  {
   "text": "Twenty-four frames from a second that never happened.",
   "t0": 45.925,
   "t1": 48.957,
   "end": 50.657,
   "n": 46
  },
  {
   "text": "Engineers checked the footage for tampering.",
   "t0": 51.157,
   "t1": 53.648,
   "end": 53.898,
   "n": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "There was none.",
   "t0": 53.898,
   "t1": 54.833,
   "end": 56.883,
   "n": 13
  },
  {
   "text": "And in every camera on Earth, the same man was standing there.",
   "t0": 57.383,
   "t1": 60.898,
   "end": 62.598,
   "n": 51
  },
  {
   "text": "On a subway platform in Tokyo.",
   "t0": 63.098,
   "t1": 64.938,
   "end": 65.188,
   "n": 25
  },
  {
   "text": "In a market in Lagos.",
   "t0": 65.308,
   "t1": 66.485,
   "end": 66.735,
   "n": 17
  },
  {
   "text": "On a farm in Iowa.",
   "t0": 66.855,
   "t1": 68.181,
   "end": 69.881,
   "n": 14
  },
  {
   "text": "Always with his back to the lens.",
   "t0": 70.381,
   "t1": 72.279,
   "end": 73.979,
   "n": 27
  },
  {
   "text": "Thousands of cameras.",
   "t0": 74.479,
   "t1": 75.885,
   "end": 76.135,
   "n": 19
  },
  {
   "text": "Thousands of cities.",
   "t0": 76.135,
   "t1": 77.463,
   "end": 77.713,
   "n": 18
  },
  {
   "text": "The same man.",
   "t0": 77.713,
   "t1": 78.488,
   "end": 78.738,
   "n": 11
  },
  {
   "text": "The same suit.",
   "t0": 78.738,
   "t1": 79.842,
   "end": 81.692,
   "n": 12
  },
  {
   "text": "Frame by frame, he was closer to the camera.",
   "t0": 82.192,
   "t1": 85.151,
   "end": 86.851,
   "n": 36
  },
  {
   "text": "And in the last frame, he had started to turn around.",
   "t0": 87.351,
   "t1": 90.699,
   "end": 92.549,
   "n": 43
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody has seen his face.",
   "t0": 93.049,
   "t1": 94.477,
   "end": 94.727,
   "n": 21
  },
  {
   "text": "The footage always ends one frame too soon.",
   "t0": 94.727,
   "t1": 97.613,
   "end": 100.463,
   "n": 36
  },
  {
   "text": "Then historians found him in older records.",
   "t0": 100.963,
   "t1": 103.627,
   "end": 105.327,
   "n": 37
  },
  {
   "text": "A monk in 1582 wrote that an hour went missing,",
   "t0": 105.827,
   "t1": 109.064,
   "end": 109.314,
   "n": 38
  },
  {
   "text": "and a man stood in every doorway.",
   "t0": 109.314,
   "t1": 111.762,
   "end": 113.612,
   "n": 27
  },
  {
   "text": "A cave painting in France shows a tall figure, turned away from the hunters.",
   "t0": 114.112,
   "t1": 118.651,
   "end": 120.501,
   "n": 63
  },
  {
   "text": "A photograph from 1888.",
   "t0": 121.001,
   "t1": 123.536,
   "end": 123.786,
   "n": 20
  },
  {
   "text": "A film reel from 1961.",
   "t0": 123.906,
   "t1": 126.685,
   "end": 128.385,
   "n": 18
  },
  {
   "text": "Every time time skipped, he was one step closer.",
   "t0": 128.885,
   "t1": 132.258,
   "end": 134.508,
   "n": 40
  },
  {
   "text": "Someone counted the steps.",
   "t0": 135.008,
   "t1": 136.655,
   "end": 139.655,
   "n": 23
  },
  {
   "text": "There is one left.",
   "t0": 140.155,
   "t1": 141.38,
   "end": 145.08,
   "n": 15
  },
  {
   "text": "When he takes it, he will be facing us.",
   "t0": 145.58,
   "t1": 148.118,
   "end": 151.818,
   "n": 31
  },
  {
   "text": "The footage was deleted within a week.",
   "t0": 152.318,
   "t1": 154.35,
   "end": 156.05,
   "n": 32
  },
  {
   "text": "Quietly, cameras around the world were turned to face the walls.",
   "t0": 156.55,
   "t1": 160.28,
   "end": 161.98,
   "n": 54
  },
  {
   "text": "Observatories stopped publishing their clock data.",
   "t0": 162.48,
   "t1": 165.497,
   "end": 167.197,
   "n": 45
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2022, the world voted to stop adding leap seconds.",
   "t0": 167.697,
   "t1": 172.013,
   "end": 173.713,
   "n": 44
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody explained why.",
   "t0": 174.213,
   "t1": 175.614,
   "end": 177.864,
   "n": 19
  },
  {
   "text": "Some people still won't look at a clock at 3:14.",
   "t0": 178.364,
   "t1": 181.852,
   "end": 183.702,
   "n": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "Some people say that at night they hear a single tick that doesn't belong to any clock.",
   "t0": 184.202,
   "t1": 188.978,
   "end": 191.828,
   "n": 71
  },
  {
   "text": "When he finally turns around, whose face will he have?",
   "t0": 192.328,
   "t1": 195.634,
   "end": 197.23399999999998,
   "n": 45
  }
 ],
